- ✅ Run the software locally for personal, non-commercial use
- ✅ Study the security implementation (Sentinel, sandbox, audit rules)
- ✅ Fork the repository for personal learning
- ✅ Submit issues, pull requests, and security reports
- ✅ Reference the code in academic papers, blog posts, or documentation
- ✅ Use the Semgrep rules and sandbox scripts for personal security audits
- ✅ Link to the project from other projects or articles

